# Corpus: commands with environment variable assignment prefixes. Three
# assignment words sit ahead of the command names (one on the first line, two on
# the second), each parsed as an Assignment, not swallowed into a word.
<<<cmd
"$PP" run std.shell --input test/suite/shellfamily/inputs/commands__5.sh --dump-tree
<<<assert
exit 0
out-absent ERROR
out-absent MISSING
out-count 3 Assignment [
out-count 2 SimpleCommand [
